{"id":49239,"ord":238,"n_segments":324,"prev":49238,"next":49240,"doc":{"id":"61539","title":"61539_Butter Jackson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Quentin Jackson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/61539/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=61539"},"chapter":"Lucky Millinder and Duke Ellington's band, 1948-52","title":"Joining Ellington at the Duke Ellington Club in Washington","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"He joined on October 21, 1948, at a short-lived Washington club; Tyree Glenn had joined over a year earlier.","period":"Oct 1948","year_from":1948,"year_to":1948,"words":94,"start":[331,1],"end":[331,14],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=61539#s49239","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Washington, D.C.","focus":1,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Duke Ellington Club","focus":1,"city":"Washington, D.C."}],"bands":[{"name":"Duke Ellington Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Duke Ellington"}]},"people":[{"name":"Duke Ellington","qid":"Q4030","n":1},{"name":"Tyree Glenn","qid":"Q488323","n":1},{"name":"Quentin Jackson","qid":"Q720707","n":1}],"story":{"theme":2,"theme_name":"Duke Ellington and his orchestra, as others knew them","community":5,"community_name":"Duke Ellington: the band, the man, his men","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":331,"b":1,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"What year was that, Butter, when you joined --"},{"p":331,"b":2,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"That was October 21, 1948."},{"p":331,"b":3,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Wow."},{"p":331,"b":4,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"That's right. And Tyree had joined the band, oh, over a year here before I got there."},{"p":331,"b":5,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"19? What year?"},{"p":331,"b":6,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"'48."},{"p":331,"b":7,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":331,"b":8,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":331,"b":9,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"What town was that in?"},{"p":331,"b":10,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"Washington, D. C."},{"p":331,"b":11,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"That's Duke's home town, huh?"},{"p":331,"b":12,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"That's right, and it was a club they tried to open called the Duke Ellington Club. It didn't last long because they couldn't get a liquor license."},{"p":331,"b":13,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":331,"b":14,"s":"MR. JACKSON","x":"But we played there. That was the most fantastic experience, to sit in that band."}]}